---
/*
 * The BEP 15 UDP announce request, packed by hand at fixed byte offsets.
 * 8 + 4 + 4 + 20 + 20 + 8 + 8 + 8 + 4 + 4 + 4 + 4 + 2 = 98.
 *
 * Boxes are to scale at 13 user units per byte, so the rows have different widths
 * and a 2-byte port really is an eighth of an 8-byte counter. Two consequences of
 * drawing it honestly: num_want is abbreviated to fit its box, and port's box is
 * too narrow for any label at all, so its name sits outside on a leader. Both
 * full names are in the <desc>, which is the text alternative.
 *
 * transaction_id carries the accent: echoing it back and verifying it against
 * every response is what makes the transport work at all.
 *
 * Shared canvas and styling: the .diagram rules in src/styles/global.css.
 */
---

<figure class="diagram">
  <div class="diagram-scroll">
    <svg
      viewBox="-8 -10 596 256"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="announce-title announce-desc"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
    >
      <title id="announce-title">Byte layout of the 98-byte BEP 15 UDP announce request</title>
      <desc id="announce-desc">
        The announce payload is 98 bytes written at fixed offsets: connection_id 8 bytes at offset 0,
        action 4, transaction_id 4, info_hash 20, peer_id 20, then the 8-byte downloaded, left and
        uploaded counters, then the 4-byte event, ip, key and num_want fields, and finally a 2-byte
        port at offset 96. The box labelled txn_id is transaction_id, and the box labelled want is
        num_want.
      </desc>

      <g class="edge-label">
        <text x="0" y="0">98 bytes, fixed offsets, packed by hand</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Row one: offsets 0 to 16 -->
      <g class="field">
        <rect x="0" y="20" width="104" height="34" rx="2" />
        <rect x="104" y="20" width="52" height="34" rx="2" />
        <text x="52" y="42" text-anchor="middle">connection_id</text>
        <text x="130" y="42" text-anchor="middle">action</text>
      </g>
      <g class="accent">
        <rect x="156" y="20" width="52" height="34" rx="2" />
        <text x="182" y="42" text-anchor="middle">txn_id</text>
      </g>
      <g class="offset">
        <text x="0" y="68" text-anchor="middle">0</text>
        <text x="104" y="68" text-anchor="middle">8</text>
        <text x="156" y="68" text-anchor="middle">12</text>
        <text x="208" y="68" text-anchor="middle">16</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Row two: offsets 16 to 56 -->
      <g class="field">
        <rect x="0" y="76" width="260" height="34" rx="2" />
        <rect x="260" y="76" width="260" height="34" rx="2" />
        <text x="130" y="98" text-anchor="middle">info_hash</text>
        <text x="390" y="98" text-anchor="middle">peer_id</text>
      </g>
      <g class="offset">
        <text x="0" y="124" text-anchor="middle">16</text>
        <text x="260" y="124" text-anchor="middle">36</text>
        <text x="520" y="124" text-anchor="middle">56</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Row three: the three 64-bit counters, offsets 56 to 80 -->
      <g class="field">
        <rect x="0" y="132" width="104" height="34" rx="2" />
        <rect x="104" y="132" width="104" height="34" rx="2" />
        <rect x="208" y="132" width="104" height="34" rx="2" />
        <text x="52" y="154" text-anchor="middle">downloaded</text>
        <text x="156" y="154" text-anchor="middle">left</text>
        <text x="260" y="154" text-anchor="middle">uploaded</text>
      </g>
      <g class="offset">
        <text x="0" y="180" text-anchor="middle">56</text>
        <text x="104" y="180" text-anchor="middle">64</text>
        <text x="208" y="180" text-anchor="middle">72</text>
        <text x="312" y="180" text-anchor="middle">80</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Row four: offsets 80 to 98. Two bytes is too narrow for the word "port". -->
      <g class="field">
        <rect x="0" y="188" width="52" height="34" rx="2" />
        <rect x="52" y="188" width="52" height="34" rx="2" />
        <rect x="104" y="188" width="52" height="34" rx="2" />
        <rect x="156" y="188" width="52" height="34" rx="2" />
        <rect x="208" y="188" width="26" height="34" rx="2" />
        <text x="26" y="210" text-anchor="middle">event</text>
        <text x="78" y="210" text-anchor="middle">ip</text>
        <text x="130" y="210" text-anchor="middle">key</text>
        <text x="182" y="210" text-anchor="middle">want</text>
      </g>
      <g class="leader">
        <line x1="236" y1="205" x2="252" y2="205" />
      </g>
      <g class="edge-label">
        <text x="258" y="210">port, 2 bytes</text>
      </g>
      <g class="offset">
        <text x="0" y="236" text-anchor="middle">80</text>
        <text x="52" y="236" text-anchor="middle">84</text>
        <text x="104" y="236" text-anchor="middle">88</text>
        <text x="156" y="236" text-anchor="middle">92</text>
        <text x="208" y="236" text-anchor="middle">96</text>
        <text x="234" y="236" text-anchor="middle">98</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    To scale at 13 units per byte. Get one offset wrong and the tracker answers, just not with peers.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
